SUMMARY:World's Appreciated Kitsch Screening time: JAWBREAKER: A Film About Anti-Cimex
DESCRIPTION:World's Appreciated Kitsch Screening time: JAWBREAKER: A Film About Anti-Cimex\nBy Tomas Haglund and Oskar Sjödin\, with English subs\, 85'\n\nThe defining documentary about the legendary Swedish punk band Anti-Cimex. Jawbreaker depicts Anti Cimex – the band that shaped Scandinavian hardcore punk and became one of Sweden’s most influential musical exports. From raw recordings in a chicken coop on the plains of Västergötland to punk scenes around the world\, the film follows a band whose uncompromising energy and political charge continue to resonate.\n\nThrough archive material\, international perspectives\, and a dreamy\, humorous tone\, directors Tomas Haglund and Oskar Sjödin paint a portrait of a musical legacy that still packs a punch!\n\nhttps://vimeo.com/913994071?fl=pl&amp\;fe=sh\n\nAnti Cimex - Scandinavian Jawbreaker LP by Cimex records\n\nPoster by @_seepsee_\n* all proceeds will be donated to the Greek Solidarity Fund of Imprisoned &amp\; Persecuted Revolutionaries\n&nbsp\;\n\nPresale/door prices adjusted: our events are set up by volunteers in favour of supporting DIY touring acts\, but it is getting ever more risky to plan and book events – please support the community and buy your tickets early! Presale closes 18.00 on day of the show.
