SUMMARY:ZACH ROWDEN (US) + ELI WENDLER (US) + URALL (BE) & MAJ RACHEL
DESCRIPTION:Charnel Ground presents: Zach Rowden (US)\, Eli Wendler (US)\, Urall (BE) &amp\; Maj Rachel\nOn the 7th of december Charnel Ground returns to OCCII\, Amsterdam for an evening of noise\, musique concrete\, electroacoustic and drone with:\n\nZach Rowden (US):\n\nZach Rowden is a musician based in New Haven\, Connecticut. His work is focused in the areas of drone\, repetitive structures and noise. Collaborators and projects include - Tongue Depressor (with Henry Birdsey)\, Hyperion Ensemble under the direction of Iancu Dumitrescu\, Red Yellow Blue Green Black (with Austin Larkin)\, Leila Bordreuil\, Aki Onda\, Arien Wilkerson\, and Paul Flaherty.\n\nEli Wendler (US):\n\nEli Wendler is a musician based in Denver Colorado\, working primarily within extreme music &amp\; touring extensively in North America and Europe. His work deals with tape manipulation\, field recordings\, repetition\, density\, trance\, resonance &amp\; the numinous. Projects include Black Curse\, Spectral Voice\, City Hunter\, Katabatic Depths\, Terravault Network.\n\nUrall (BE):\n\nCrude tape and sound collage by Jim Faes combining field recordings\, tape loops and broken synthesizers. Urall released work on such labels as Throne Heap\, Dadaist Tapes and White Centipede Noise.\n\nMaj Rachel:\n\nMaj Rachel is a composer and experimental sound artist. She combines her voice with ambient/noise compositions in which she records objects as percussion\, machine sounds and field recordings of her surroundings.
CATEGORIES:music
LOCATION:#_LOCATIONNAME\, #_LOCATIONFULLLINE\, #_LOCATIONCOUNTRY
URL:https://occii.org/events/charnel-ground-71226/
X-RDR-COST;X-RDR-CURRENCY=EUR:10
