SUMMARY:Ragdawl presents: “Split Tape” Album Release w/ The Medicines\, Lifeless Past & Raw Desire + DJ Duo NO FUN
DESCRIPTION:Ragdawl presents: “Split Tape” Album Release w/ The Medicines\, Lifeless Past &amp\; Raw Desire + DJ NO FUN\n\n\nSplit Tape brings together three post-punk bands from the Netherlands: Amsterdam’s Raw Desire\, The Hague’s Lifeless Past and Almere’s The Medicines. This six-track split release explores three distinct takes on post-punk\, capturing the diversity of the Dutch underground scene.\n\nThe Medicines\n\nEmerging from Almere\, The Netherlands\, The Medicines are a guitar-wave band blending dark\, brooding vocals with effect-driven staccato guitar\, energetic bass\, and psychedelic synthesizers. Influenced by the 1980s alternative music scene\, their sound bridges the past and present while retaining their distinctive style. The Medicines’ debut album ‘Shine Through The Darkness’ was released in 2025 through Violet Hour Transmissions (USA).\n\n\n\nhttps://themedicinesmusic.bandcamp.com/\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xQbMEB2PJ6I\n\nLifeless Past\n\nLifeless Past is a creative manifestation born from disillusionment and rebellion. Their music is fueled by drum machines and led by ethereal yet provoking guitars\, creating an unparalleled musical landscape. Their sound is often described as dark\, enchanting and liberating. Lifeless Past was founded in the early 2010’s by producer and multi-instrumentalist Satori. The current live lineup consists of Satori ( guitars\, programming and vocals) together with Maurice on electronic percussion.\n\nhttps://lifelesspast.bandcamp.com/\nhttps://www.instagram.com/lifelesspast\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n1g03LTnBqA\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nRaw Desire\nSharp melodic riffs\, cold basslines\, and constant anxious tension define Raw Desire’s take on Postpunk. Dark\, urgent\, and edged with punk rawness\, their sound thrives on unease and momentum.\n\n\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/rawdesire_/\nhttps://rawdesire.bandcamp.com/\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nNO FUN – DJ\nNO FUN found each other among the record bins at Concerto\, bonded by a shared love for melancholic wave\, garage\, synth-pop\, and forgotten 80s gems.\n\n\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nPresale/door prices adjusted: our events are set up by volunteers in favour of supporting DIY touring acts\, but it is getting ever more risky to plan and book events – please support the community and buy your tickets early! Presale end at 18:00 on day of the show. No tickets at the door if the show is sold out online
